 tresc_en: |
-  Dr inż. **Błażej Wróbel** of the Mathematical Institute of the University of Wrocław has received the [Polish Mathematical Society Prize for Young Mathematicians](http://www.ptm.org.pl/zawartosc/b%C5%82a%C5%BCej-wr%C3%B3bel-laureatem-nagrody-ptm-dla-m%C5%82odych-matematyk%C3%B3w-za-2014) for a series of six papers in harmonic analysis and operator theory.
+  Dr **Błażej Wróbel** of the Mathematical Institute of the University of Wrocław has received the [Polish Mathematical Society Prize for Young Mathematicians](http://www.ptm.org.pl/zawartosc/b%C5%82a%C5%BCej-wr%C3%B3bel-laureatem-nagrody-ptm-dla-m%C5%82odych-matematyk%C3%B3w-za-2014) for a series of six papers in harmonic analysis and operator theory.
 
   The awarded papers make a significant contribution to the theory of multivariate multipliers for commuting operators and of general Riesz transforms. Particularly noteworthy is the solution of open problems concerning the validity of Marcinkiewicz-type theorems for systems of commuting operators, including those related to the system of Ornstein–Uhlenbeck operators.
 zaklad: "analiza-funkcjonalna"
